Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:49:37

Fixed. The GPU Governor test no longer names another board: it warns that a GPU governor "made for another board" is
installed, and the IOMMU test and the benchmark's help say the same without it. The benchmark's comparison list
loses that board's row. The Wi-Fi Adapter test (53) is the PS5's built-in Wi-Fi alone, its driver and firmware: the
reader of every other adapter went, as its hints named an app this suite does not have. The two system score tiles,
which were never shown on a PS5, are removed from the code. The older entries here no longer name that board.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:35:42

Release 0.2.1.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:48:09

Fixed. The app's icon is its category's current picture.

Changelog: 11-11-2026

Release 0.2.0. The diagnostics (the window, the test
runner, the results and the history, and test-bazzite.sh). PS5 versions of the hardware tests: platform (DMI
PlayStation 5, the ps5-linux kernel's PS5 drivers, the loader's bzImage), GPU governor and clock scaling (the kernel's
ps5-gpufreq devfreq instead of an SMU governor), CU count (36), sensors (ps5_fan), IOMMU (information only),
mitigations (advice), CPU cores (8C/16T), CPU power (no cpufreq; ps5-linux-tools' boost), suspend (s2idle), display
(the PS5 HDMI state), VRAM (/boot/efi/vram.txt), throttling, HDMI-CEC (ps5-cec), Wi-Fi (the IW620 on moal), updates
on a flattened image (dnf). Dropped: CPU voltage (no SuperIO). Later, with PS5 baselines: the stress test,
the benchmark, the system score and the game page (ported, hidden). The core gets the Wi-Fi reader (wifi.py); a
switched-off Wi-Fi while a cable network is up is a note, not a warning.

